```
=============================================================
Detection: System Binary Proxy Execution - process creation (Sysmon EID 1)
           correlated with outbound network connection (Sysmon EID 3).
Technique: T1218.005 (mshta) / .010 (regsvr32) / .011 (rundll32) - one holistic rule
Tactic:    Defence Evasion (TA0005)
Platform:  Splunk SPL. Counterpart to rule.yml (Sigma base, process_creation).
Data:      XmlWinEventLog/Sysmon: EventCode 1 (process creation) + 3 (network connection)
Author:    William Richardson   Date: 2026-07-19  (V2 - complete; tier cuts lowered post-SPL testing)

Detects three signed system binaries - mshta, regsvr32, rundll32 - being abused to
proxy execution of malicious code past application control and signature defences.
One row per proxy-binary process (ProcessGuid): the EID 1 event carries the command
line / parent-child signals, the EID 3 event (same ProcessGuid) carries the network
flag. Grouping by ProcessGuid folds both together with max() - a signal that fired on
the process-creation event survives the collapse, an EID 3 row scores 0 on its own.

SCOPE
  Sees the proxy binary AS the process (Image = mshta/regsvr32/rundll32) and its own
  outbound connections. mshta/rundll32/regsvr32 chaining between each other is caught by
  the parent signals. A proxy binary spawning a *shell* (mshta -> powershell/cmd) is
  deliberately OUT OF SCOPE - that child-execution chain belongs to a T1059.001 rule,
  which correlates parents/grandparents. Renamed binaries are caught via OriginalFileName
  on EID 1, but a renamed binary's EID 3 won't match the image filter (rare edge case).

FIRING LOGIC (weighted score - see SEVERITY block)
  Critical = Score >= 5     High = Score 4     Medium = Score 2-3     Informational = Score 1
  Informational sits BELOW the firing floor (where Score >= 2), i.e. a lone weak signal is
  graded but never surfaced. Drop the floor to >= 1 if you want to see those for hunting.
  A network connection only counts when a process-creation signal is already present -
  a bare proxy binary calling out with no other signal does not fire on its own.

SIGNAL WEIGHTS
  Smoking guns (4): cred_dump (comsvcs MiniDump), squiblydoo_remote (/i:http|ftp). High on
                    their own, Critical with a second signal or a network hit. Credential
                    dumping is network-independent, so it does not wait on a connection.
  Strong (2):       rundll_script_abuse, mshta_cli, mshta_clsid, mshta_parent,
                    squiblydoo_local, regsvr_parent. Medium alone, Critical + network.
  Weak (1):         rundll_parent, path_obfuscation. Never fire alone; the
                    rundll_parent + path_obfuscation combo = 2 (mirrors the Sigma condition).
  Network (+3):     added once, only when SignalScore >= 1.

TUNING
  Raise the floor to Score >= 4 to keep only High/Critical if the rundll32/regsvr32 baseline is
  noisy. Note a single strong signal + a network hit = 5 = Critical, skipping High; drop the
  network bonus to +2 if that grades too hard.
  rundll_parent lists common shells (cmd/powershell) on purpose - it is weight 1 and
  cannot fire alone, so a legitimate shell -> rundll32 stays silent unless it also loads a
  DLL by ordinal / from a user-writable path, or the process calls out to the network.

ASSUMES Splunk_TA_windows auto-extracts Image / ParentImage / CommandLine / OriginalFileName /
ProcessGuid / User / Destination* from the Sysmon channel. #1 SPL GOTCHA: SPL collapses "\\" to a
single "\" before the regex engine sees it, so never anchor a match() on a path separator ("\\name").
"\\m" becomes the invalid escape "\m" and errors the whole search; "\\r" silently matches a carriage
return and never fires. Anchor on the file name instead ("name\.exe$"), as proc / *_parent do below.
A single "\." for a literal dot is safe (dot is not a letter). Triple-backtick comments need Splunk 8.1+.
=============================================================```
index=sysmon (EventCode=1 OR EventCode=3)
 (Image="*\\mshta.exe" OR Image="*\\rundll32.exe" OR Image="*\\regsvr32.exe"
     OR OriginalFileName IN ("MSHTA.EXE","RUNDLL32.EXE","REGSVR32.EXE"))

``` which proxy binary is this - keyed off Image, falling back to OriginalFileName so a
    renamed binary is still classified on its EID 1 event ```
| eval proc = case(
        match(Image,"(?i)rundll32\.exe$") OR OriginalFileName=="RUNDLL32.EXE", "rundll32",
        match(Image,"(?i)mshta\.exe$")    OR OriginalFileName=="MSHTA.EXE",    "mshta",
        match(Image,"(?i)regsvr32\.exe$") OR OriginalFileName=="REGSVR32.EXE", "regsvr32",
        true(), "unknown")

``` network flag - carried on the EID 3 event, folded onto the process by max() below ```
| eval isNetwork = if(EventCode==3, 1, 0)

``` --- SIGNALS (per-event; each gated to its binary so a token shared across binaries -
    e.g. javascript: - is only scored once. EID 3 rows have null CommandLine/ParentImage
    so they score 0 and are picked up from the EID 1 event by max()). ------------------- ```

``` rundll32 ```
| eval rundll_script_abuse = if(proc=="rundll32" AND match(CommandLine, "(?i)(javascript:|vbscript:|mshtml\s*,\s*RunHTMLApplication|mshtml\s*,\s*ShowHTMLDialog|shell32\.dll\s*,\s*ShellExec_RunDLL|zipfldr\.dll\s*,\s*RouteTheCall|url\.dll\s*,\s*OpenURL|url\.dll\s*,\s*FileProtocolHandler|advpack\.dll\s*,\s*LaunchINFSection|setupapi\.dll\s*,\s*InstallHinfSection|pcwutl\.dll\s*,\s*LaunchApplication)"), 1, 0)
| eval cred_dump         = if(proc=="rundll32" AND match(CommandLine, "(?i)comsvcs(\.dll)?\s*,\s*(#\+?24|minidump)"), 1, 0)
| eval path_obfuscation  = if(proc=="rundll32" AND match(CommandLine, "(?i)(\.dll\s*,\s*#|%TEMP%|%APPDATA%|%PUBLIC%|Users.Public.|AppData.Local.Temp.|Downloads.)"), 1, 0)
| eval rundll_parent     = if(proc=="rundll32" AND match(ParentImage, "(?i)(mshta|regsvr32|outlook|winword|excel|cmd|powershell|pwsh|wscript|cscript)\.exe$"), 1, 0)

``` mshta ```
| eval mshta_parent      = if(proc=="mshta" AND match(ParentImage, "(?i)(outlook|winword|excel|powerpnt|chrome|msedge|firefox)\.exe$"), 1, 0)
| eval mshta_cli         = if(proc=="mshta" AND match(CommandLine, "(?i)(javascript:|vbscript:|https?://|GetObject\(|ActiveXObject|CreateObject\(|\.Run\(| -enc|FromBase64String)"), 1, 0)
| eval mshta_clsid       = if(proc=="mshta" AND match(CommandLine, "(?i)\{[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}\}"), 1, 0)

``` regsvr32 - squiblydoo_remote (a /i:URL) is near-zero-FP; the local scrobj/.sct case is
    strong but not conclusive, and is suppressed when the remote flag already fired so the
    same command line is not counted twice. ```
| eval regsvr_parent     = if(proc=="regsvr32" AND match(ParentImage, "(?i)(rundll32|mshta|outlook|winword|excel|chrome|msedge|firefox|wscript|cscript)\.exe$"), 1, 0)
| eval squiblydoo_remote = if(proc=="regsvr32" AND match(CommandLine, "(?i)/i:(http|ftp)"), 1, 0)
| eval squiblydoo_local  = if(proc=="regsvr32" AND match(CommandLine, "(?i)(scrobj\.dll|\.sct)") AND squiblydoo_remote==0, 1, 0)

``` --- collapse to one row per process; max() carries any fired signal + the network flag
    across the EID 1 / EID 3 events that share this ProcessGuid --- ```
| stats max(cred_dump) as cred_dump max(squiblydoo_remote) as squiblydoo_remote
        max(rundll_script_abuse) as rundll_script_abuse max(mshta_cli) as mshta_cli
        max(mshta_clsid) as mshta_clsid max(mshta_parent) as mshta_parent
        max(squiblydoo_local) as squiblydoo_local max(regsvr_parent) as regsvr_parent
        max(rundll_parent) as rundll_parent max(path_obfuscation) as path_obfuscation
        max(isNetwork) as has_network
        values(proc) as proc values(CommandLine) as CommandLine
        values(ParentImage) as ParentImage values(Image) as Image values(User) as User
        values(ParentProcessGuid) as ParentProcessGuid values(DestinationIp) as DestinationIp
        values(DestinationPort) as DestinationPort values(DestinationHostname) as DestinationHostname
        min(_time) as StartTime
        by ProcessGuid, Computer

``` --- SEVERITY - weighted score. Network adds +3 but only when a process-creation signal
    is already present, so a proxy binary calling out with nothing else stays silent. --- ```
| eval SignalScore = (cred_dump*4) + (squiblydoo_remote*4)
                   + (rundll_script_abuse*2) + (mshta_cli*2) + (mshta_clsid*2) + (mshta_parent*2)
                   + (squiblydoo_local*2) + (regsvr_parent*2)
                   + (rundll_parent*1) + (path_obfuscation*1)
| eval Score = SignalScore + if(SignalScore>=1 AND has_network==1, 3, 0)
| eval Severity = case(Score>=5, "Critical", Score>=4, "High", Score>=2, "Medium", Score>=1, "Informational", true(), "None")

``` firing floor - Score 1 (a lone weak signal) is graded Informational but never surfaced.
    Raise to >= 4 to keep only High/Critical; drop to >= 1 to surface Informational for hunting ```
| where Score >= 2

``` --- analyst-facing reason (first match wins -> highest / most-specific signal first) --- ```
| eval DetectionReason = case(
        cred_dump==1,           "rundll32 comsvcs.dll MiniDump - LSASS credential-dump export",
        squiblydoo_remote==1,   "regsvr32 fetching a remote scriptlet (/i:http|ftp) - Squiblydoo remote payload",
        rundll_script_abuse==1, "rundll32 proxying execution via a script engine / dangerous DLL export",
        mshta_clsid==1,         "mshta invoked with a bare COM CLSID instead of a file path",
        mshta_cli==1,           "mshta command line carries inline script / remote URL / encoded payload",
        mshta_parent==1,        "mshta spawned by an Office app or browser - typical phishing delivery",
        squiblydoo_local==1,    "regsvr32 loading a local scriptlet (scrobj.dll / .sct)",
        regsvr_parent==1,       "regsvr32 spawned by a script host, Office app or browser",
        (rundll_parent==1 AND path_obfuscation==1), "rundll32 from a shell/proxy parent loading a DLL by ordinal or from a user-writable path",
        path_obfuscation==1,    "rundll32 loading a DLL by ordinal or from a user-writable path",
        rundll_parent==1,       "rundll32 spawned by a shell, Office app or proxy binary",
        true(),                 "suspicious proxy-binary execution")
| eval DetectionReason = if(has_network==1, DetectionReason . "; process also made an outbound network connection", DetectionReason)

``` every signal that fired, so the analyst sees exactly what stacked into the score ```
| eval Signals = mvappend(
        if(cred_dump==1,"cred_dump",null()), if(squiblydoo_remote==1,"squiblydoo_remote",null()),
        if(rundll_script_abuse==1,"rundll_script_abuse",null()), if(mshta_cli==1,"mshta_cli",null()),
        if(mshta_clsid==1,"mshta_clsid",null()), if(mshta_parent==1,"mshta_parent",null()),
        if(squiblydoo_local==1,"squiblydoo_local",null()), if(regsvr_parent==1,"regsvr_parent",null()),
        if(rundll_parent==1,"rundll_parent",null()), if(path_obfuscation==1,"path_obfuscation",null()))

| eval StartTime = strftime(StartTime, "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")
| table StartTime, Computer, Severity, Score, proc, DetectionReason, Signals, User,
        ParentImage, Image, CommandLine, has_network, DestinationIp, DestinationPort,
        DestinationHostname, ProcessGuid, ParentProcessGuid
| sort - Score, - StartTime

```
------------------------------------------------------------
FALSE POSITIVES / TUNING
  regsvr32 - legitimate COM/DLL registration by installers launched from a script host
             (local file path, no /i:URL, no scrobj.dll). Watch for SCCM/Intune deployment
             bursts hitting many hosts at once.
  mshta    - legacy internal HTA-based admin tools and line-of-business apps.
  rundll32 - biggest FP source: Control Panel routing, printer mgmt, installers running INF
             sections via advpack/setupapi, updaters loading vendor DLLs from %TEMP%/%APPDATA%.
             Weak signals (rundll_parent / path_obfuscation) never fire alone for this reason.

ANALYST TRIAGE
  Pivot fields: Computer, ProcessGuid, ParentProcessGuid, User, Image.
  1. Read Signals + DetectionReason - what actually fired, and did it also call out (has_network)?
  2. Decode any encoded/remote payload on CommandLine:
       powershell -c "[Text.Encoding]::Unicode.GetString([Convert]::FromBase64String('<blob>'))"
  3. If has_network=1, triage Destination* - internal/known-good vs. external/unknown. No IP/host
     allow-list is baked in (keeps the rule portable); scope it against your own infra.
  4. Walk the chain by GUID - ParentProcessGuid upward (who launched the proxy binary) and any
     children downward. mshta/rundll32 -> shell handoff is out of scope here; pivot to T1059.001.
  5. Confirmed malicious -> isolate the host, capture the command line + any referenced payload,
     hunt the same Image/CommandLine across other hosts, begin DFIR.
     Benign -> add User + CommandLine to the tuning allow-list.
------------------------------------------------------------
```
